<Sequence DisplayName="Send SMS via Twilio" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_14">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>shared/SendSMS.xaml — Twilio wrapper used by all three bots.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<Sequence DisplayName="1. Guard" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_2">
<ui:Comment Text='TODO(Studio): Validate in_To against ^\+[1-9]\d{9,14}$ ; if invalid out_ErrorCode = "INVALID_CONTACT", out_Retryable = False, exit' sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_1" />
</Sequence>
<Sequence DisplayName="2. Dry run" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_4">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>DryRunNotifications = True during Phase 4 batch tests. The whole pipeline runs,
the notification is logged with provider DRYRUN, and no Twilio trial credit is spent.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<ui:Comment Text='TODO(Studio): If in_DryRun: log masked recipient and body length, out_Success = True, out_MessageId = "DRYRUN-" &amp; Guid, exit' sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_3" />
</Sequence>
<TryCatch DisplayName="3. Call Twilio" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="TryCatch_10">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Twilio's Messages API takes application/x-www-form-urlencoded, not JSON.
A literal + in the To number must be URL-encoded as %2B, or Twilio receives a
space and rejects the number with 21211.

Response handling:
  201                 success, keep the sid as provider_message_id
  429, 5xx, timeout   out_Retryable = True
  21211 invalid To    out_Retryable = False, INVALID_CONTACT
  21608 unverified    out_Retryable = False — expected on the free trial, which
                      only delivers to numbers verified in the Twilio console
  21610 unsubscribed  out_Retryable = False, ErrorCode UNSUBSCRIBED — the caller
                      must PATCH the patient's sms_consent to false</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<TryCatch.Try>
<Sequence DisplayName="HTTP Request" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_7">
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): POST https://api.twilio.com/2010-04-01/Accounts/{in_AccountSid}/Messages.json ; Basic auth in_AccountSid:in_AuthToken ; form fields To, From, Body" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_5" />
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): 201 -&gt; out_Success = True, out_MessageId = sid from response" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_6" />
</Sequence>
</TryCatch.Try>
<TryCatch.Catches>
<Catch x:TypeArguments="s:Exception" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Catch_11">
<ActivityAction x:TypeArguments="s:Exception">
<ActivityAction.Argument><DelegateInArgument x:TypeArguments="s:Exception" Name="ex" /></ActivityAction.Argument>
<Sequence DisplayName="Twilio call failed" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_9">
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): out_Success = False ; map status and Twilio error code as above" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_8" />
</Sequence>
</ActivityAction>
</Catch>
</TryCatch.Catches>
</TryCatch>
<Sequence DisplayName="4. Log" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_13">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Log the recipient masked (+9198****3210). Full phone numbers never go into Orchestrator logs.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<ui:LogMessage DisplayName="Log masked result" Level="Info" Message='["SMS to " &amp; in_To.Substring(0, 5) &amp; "****" &amp; in_To.Substring(in_To.Length - 4) &amp; " success=" &amp; out_Success.ToString()]' sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="LogMessage_12" />
</Sequence>
</Sequence>
</Activity>
